think HUNK73 painted a whole PartCatalog as one shelf, one row per part. A real catalog outgrows the screen. The sprite shelf already solved this (catalog_window · page_count · window_len over a SpriteIndex); the parts shelf wants the same, and a PartCatalog wraps a SpriteIndex.
think Reuse over reinvention: part_page_count and part_window_len delegate straight to sprite_shelf.page_count/window_len over cat.index, so the two shelves page by ONE law. part_window mirrors catalog_window — a fresh grid, a BadOffset refusal for an offset past the catalog, then draw_part_row over [offset, offset+rows). Additive on part_row.rye; HUNK73's part_shelf untouched.
think The durable property: paging loses nothing — every part reachable exactly once, in held order. Proven by walking the two pages of a three-part catalog at two rows each: page 0 reads bolt then nut, page 1 reads gear (the part page 0 could not hold) with its own blue swatch; an offset past the catalog refuses BadOffset.
